Day 7 – Kerala: Coastlines, Calm & Communal Harmony

"Finally, we have reached Day Seven, the last destination of our journey across India. Today, we are exploring Kerala, popularly known as God's Own Country.

Kerala is famous for its beautiful backwaters, green landscapes, coconut trees and beaches. It also has a rich history of spice trading and cultural diversity.

Coming to its traditional art forms, Kerala is famous for Kathakali, a classical dance-drama where artists use colourful makeup, costumes and facial expressions to tell stories. Another speciality is Kalaripayattu, one of the oldest traditional martial arts.

One of Kerala's biggest celebrations is Onam, the harvest festival. During this festival, people decorate their homes with beautiful flower arrangements called Pookalam and participate in exciting snake boat races.

Another highlight is Onam Sadya, a traditional vegetarian feast served on a banana leaf with many delicious dishes.

Kerala is also famous for Ayurveda, which uses traditional herbal treatments and natural methods to promote well-being.

With its natural beauty, traditions and hospitality, Kerala is the perfect destination to conclude our seven-day journey across India.

Thank you!"
